      "side": 0,
      "message": "If I back out the config_allowed.txt changes and add the below diff per your suggestion, I get the same error message listed previously when building ECOS helipilot, please let me know if I\u0027ve misunderstood. As a minore not, to get past the CQ failures, think we\u0027d be required to add the changes to get past them to this CL and not another one...unless you are thinking I keep the config_allowed changes in this CL and then back them out in the the next CL in the chain which also fixes the CQ and EC compilation failures?\n\n```\ndiff --git a/include/config.h b/include/config.h\nindex 166a27676f..d4f76aee09 100644\n--- a/include/config.h\n+++ b/include/config.h\n@@ -3792,6 +3792,9 @@\n /* Support One Time Protection structure */\n #undef CONFIG_OTP\n \n+/* Support additional key in OTP memory */\n+#undef CONFIG_OTP_KEY\n+\n```",
